---
import LaunchLayout from "../layouts/LaunchLayout.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, REPOSITORY } from "../config/launch";
---
<LaunchLayout title="Trust, data & deployment boundaries | Velvet" description="How to evaluate Velvet: self-hosted scope, evidence assumptions, pilot data handling, website privacy, and private vulnerability reporting.">
  <div class="l-wrap l-page"><div class="l-page-head"><p class="l-eyebrow">Trust &amp; data</p><h1>Know the boundary<br />before relying on it.</h1><p class="l-lede">Velvet is currently local and self-hosted. A successful demonstration is not an independent security audit, a certification, or a blanket assurance for your deployment.</p></div>
    <div class="l-grid"><article class="l-card"><h3>What is available</h3><p>Open-source implementation, public reference evidence, assisted staging evaluations, and supported enforcement components. Review the exact source revision and integration before adoption.</p></article><article class="l-card"><h3>What is not promised</h3><p>A hosted enterprise service, universal agent safety, complete MCP protocol coverage, round-the-clock incident response, or certification of your environment.</p></article><article class="l-card"><h3>What the evidence needs</h3><p>Explicit route inventory, trustworthy observers, independently pinned public keys, controlled executor credentials, and review of the actual deployment assumptions.</p></article></div>
    <section class="l-page-section l-prose"><h2>Before a pilot receives access</h2><p>Agree the authorized scope and use customer-controlled staging or a representative hermetic fixture. Use synthetic records and narrowly scoped test credentials. Do not send secrets through the contact page or a public issue.</p><p>Identify who operates the observer and holds signing keys. Review what the report might reveal even when raw prompts are absent. Agree artifact location, permitted access, redaction, retention, deletion, and access removal in the written scope before sharing data.</p><p>The starting offer does not require production credentials, production balances, or live customer records. Additional security or procurement requirements must be resolved before the engagement starts.</p></section>
    <section class="l-page-section l-prose"><h2>Website and contact privacy</h2><p>The contact page prepares a draft in your browser. It does not post the form to a Velvet lead database. Nothing is sent by that form until you choose to use your email application and send the message. The copy button writes only to your clipboard at your request.</p><p>The recorded replay uses a small allowlist of aggregate interaction event names. Its application event payload does not include your draft, prompts, email address, or arbitrary properties. Other commercial pages do not add a third-party analytics tracker.</p><p>The site is configured for Cloudflare hosting. Hosting and email providers may process operational request metadata and correspondence under their own service arrangements. This page does not claim those providers collect no personal information.</p><p>For questions about an inquiry or data shared directly with Paul, contact <a class="l-contact-link" href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Customer-specific data arrangements are agreed separately.</p></section>
    <section class="l-page-section l-prose"><h2>Report a security concern privately</h2><p>Use the repository's private vulnerability-reporting channel. Do not post credentials, exploitation details, private customer data, or an undisclosed third-party finding in a public issue.</p><div class="l-actions"><a class="l-button" href={`${REPOSITORY}/security/advisories/new`}>Private vulnerability report ↗</a><a class="l-button l-button-quiet" href={`${REPOSITORY}/blob/main/SECURITY.md`}>Read the security policy</a></div></section>
    <p class="l-fine">Reference documents: <a href={`${REPOSITORY}/blob/main/IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md`}>implementation status</a> · <a href={`${REPOSITORY}/blob/main/docs/liability/VELVET_ROPE_PUBLIC_CLAIMS_POLICY.md`}>public claims policy</a> · <a href="/evidence/">evidence boundaries</a>.</p>
  </div>
</LaunchLayout>
